maternal age and gestational age were selected, and their archived first or second trimester serum retrieved for AMH 
assay.   Results There was no significant difference in maternal serum AMH level between pregnancies affected and 
unaffected by foetal Down syndrome. Our first trimester serum samples had higher AMH concentration compared to second 
trimester samples.
