- Study 93: NTplus method combining early PAPP-A, NT, and later triple test

EXCLUDED STUDIES (91):
Studies were excluded for the following reasons:
- Single trimester only (first OR second trimester markers without combination)
- Single marker evaluation studies
- Review articles and meta-analyses
- Studies focusing on adjustment factors (weight, smoking, ethnicity)
- Ultrasound-only studies
- Molecular diagnostic methods (cfDNA, PCR)
- Studies not evaluating screening performance
- Studies on other conditions or unrelated topics

### 3. Additional context:
The screening was conservative - studies were included when they evaluated any form of combined first and second 
trimester screening approach (integrated, contingent, serial, or cross-trimester). Studies evaluating only first 
trimester OR only second trimester screening were excluded as they do not meet the criteria of COMBINING both 
trimesters. Review articles were excluded as they are not primary studies evaluating screening performance.
